<overview>
<p>Firefighting platoons carry portable fire-suppression gear and breathing aparatus for responding to fires on the battlefield, on base, and in civilian areas. These engineers combat fires ignited by inferno munitions, fuel explosions, and energy weapon strikes that threaten friendly positions or civilian infrastructure. Their reliance on supplied transport for movement and lack of armament outside of Halligan tools as improvised clubs means they are unlikely to be encountered outside of friendly facilities and escorted salvage operations.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date selected as generic early date, prior to most advanced infantry equipment
</notes>

